{"authored" [{"question" "q-106704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/assets/5bd3bf7cecf806ab0fc89db59afc5d385064080f47076d13d2ef25650ce39a23.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate the ellipse shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e17fbd21a60b56f03ed40cebf7ae0d2f64b16f2af961e0289f78fb903d56fc" "basis" 1107 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(3,-2),$ $a=3$ and $b=8.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7e17fbd21a60b56f03ed40cebf7ae0d2f64b16f2af961e0289f78fb903d56fc" "basis" 1107 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd3c3ab57d3f4eee40fa133cc881384f001d3a25c4d860095ddb8674be6cfd